Raises ValueError if the value is not present.␀␀D.insert(index, object) -- insert object before index␀AÀŠ¼WRemove and return the rightmost element.␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Remove and return the leftmost element.␀A ‹¼&Return state information for pickling.␀AÐ‹¼4D.remove(value) -- remove first occurrence of value.␀AŒ¼aD.__reversed__() -- return a reverse iterator over the deque␀␀␀␀D.reverse() -- reverse *IN PLACE*␀A€¼URotate the deque n steps to the right (default n=1).  If n is negative, rotates left.␀Aà¼D.__sizeof__() -- size of D in memory, in bytes␀defaultdict(default_factory=None, /, [...]) --> dict with default factory

The default factory is called without arguments to produce
a new value when a key is not present, in __getitem__ only.
A defaultdict compares equal to a dict with the same items.
All remaining arguments are treated the same as if they were
