Resets the cache and forces GL state to known defaults.

This should only be called when the GL context is valid.␀A†ãÁnew_context(self, core_profile: bool) -> void

Forgets everything cached about the previous context, without making GL
calls, as GL may not be loaded yet. The cache then matches a newly created
context. A reused context may hold other state, so callers must also call
reset() once GL is loaded and the default VAO exists.␀AàˆãP__pyx_unpickle_GLStateCache(__pyx_type, __pyx_checksum: int, __pyx_state: tuple)␀AÀ‰ãå	Êe␀Êe␀Êe␀␀␀␀␀blend_dst_alpha, blend_dst_rgb, blend_eq_alpha, blend_eq_rgb, blend_src_alpha, blend_src_rgb, buffer_frame, buffer_generation, color_mask_a, color_mask_b, color_mask_g, color_mask_r, core_profile, current_active_texture, current_array_buffer, current_element_buffer, current_program, current_texture, enabled_attrib_mask, reset_serial, scratch_buffers␀9␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀)␀␀␀␀␀␀³␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀	␀␀␀	␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀	␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀&␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀!␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀
