This is Ren'Py specific, and implements a subset of the pygame threshold API.

This computes the differences in a and b. Pixels that are the same in a are set to same_color in
dest, and pixels that are different are set to different_color.

dest, a, ab and b must all be the same size and format.

same_color and different_color may be any color accepted by map_color().

Returns the count of different pixels.␀AÞê`Qf␀8Qf␀PQf␀¬Qf␀xQf␀A°Þê0flip(surface: Surface, xbool: bool, ybool: bool)␀AðÞêwàQf␀èQf␀ðQf␀␀␀␀␀scale(surface: Surface, size, DestSurface: Surface = None)␀␀␀␀␀␀rotate(surface: Surface, angle)␀àQf␀HQf␀AðßêGrotozoom(surface: Surface, angle: float, scale: float, smooth: int = 1)␀AÀàêàQf␀HQf␀°Qf␀ÄQf␀Aààê@smoothscale(surface: Surface, size, DestSurface: Surface = None)␀A°áêàQf␀ÀQf␀Qf␀␀␀␀␀4␀␀␀ð␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀	␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀³␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀'␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀	␀␀␀␀␀␀>␀␀␀A␀␀␀␀␀␀E␀␀␀8␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀)␀␀␀+␀␀␀␀␀␀	␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀
